INT. SILVERADO HOTEL - BATHHOUSE - DAY

Steam. Brass taps, a copper tub, white tile gone yellow with age. A kettle simmers on a wood stove. A pocket-watch lies on a stool, ticking too loud.

ABNER CALLOWAY, 50s, a grey mustache and a hat he won't take off, sits in the tub with his arms along the rim, eyes shut. His younger partner CALEB DREWRY, 30s, rolls up his sleeves at the stove, sloshing a pot of water.

ABNER
You're slow.

CALEB
You're hot.

ABNER
That's the point of a bath, son.

Caleb pours. Steam billows. Abner exhales, sinks lower.

CALEB
He's here.

ABNER
Who?

CALEB
Isaiah.

Abner opens one eye.

ABNER
Where?

CALEB
Downstairs. Drinking.

ABNER
Alone?

CALEB
With Hesper.

ABNER
Hm.

HESPER VANCE, 20s, in a pressed shirt and a leather vest, leans in the doorway with a cup of coffee, a silver star on her chest. ISAIAH RUTHERFORD, 40s, in a black coat, steps in behind her, hat low, holding a short shotgun by the barrel.

HESPER
Don't get up, Calloway.

ABNER
Wasn't planning on it.

ISAIAH
You boys been busy.

CALEB
Not as busy as you.

ISAIAH
Hm.

He stands very still. The kettle sings. Hesper sips. The pocket-watch ticks. Abner moves one hand, slow, under the soapy water.

HESPER
Whatever's under there, leave it.

ABNER
It's a bar of soap.

HESPER
Leave the soap.

Abner raises his hand, empty. A grin splits his beard.

ABNER
Sheriff, you're a hard woman.

HESPER
Marshal.

ABNER
Beg your pardon.

ISAIAH
Calloway. You know why I'm here.

ABNER
Money.

ISAIAH
Yes.

ABNER
It's in the stove.

Caleb drops the pot. Hesper's eyes flick to the fire. Isaiah steps toward it. In one smooth motion, Abner lunges up, soaking wet, a pistol in his fist, and fires.

The lamp explodes. Darkness. Steam. A scream, a crash of copper, a gunshot, another.

When the smoke clears, the tub is empty. The window is open. Curtains lift. Hesper stands at the sill, coffee spilled down her vest. Isaiah picks the shotgun up off the tile.

ISAIAH
He took the soap.
